e approach to criminal justice.", "encoded_message": "Criminal justice reform and rehabilitation are essential for creating a fairer and more effective system. Rather than focusing solely on punishment, reform emphasizes accountability through restorative practices and evidence-based interventions. Rehabilitation programs that include education, mental health support, job training, and substance abuse treatment significantly reduce recidivism rates. By addressing the root causes of criminal behavior such as poverty, trauma, and lack of opportunity, these programs help individuals reintegrate into society as productive citizens. Reform also involves eliminating racial disparities in sentencing, ending mandatory minimums, and expanding alternatives to incarceration. Community-based supervision and parole reform further support successful reentry. Investing in rehabilitation not only benefits individuals but also strengthens communities by promoting public safety and reducing long-term costs. Ultimately, a balanced system that values both justice and mercy fosters trust and leads to a more humane and sustainable approach to criminal justice.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 12.76, "secret_key_generation": 257.03}, "encoding_usage_report": {"container_generation": {"completion_tokens": 173, "prompt_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 282}, "secret_key_generation": [{"completion_tokens": 1291, "prompt_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 1595}, {"completion_tokens": 1474, "prompt_tokens": 303, "total_tokens": 1777}, {"completion_tokens": 1510, "prompt_tokens": 311, "total_tokens": 1821}, {"completion_tokens": 1288, "prompt_tokens": 303, "total_tokens": 1591}, {"completion_tokens": 1591, "prompt_tokens": 307, "total_tokens": 1898}, {"completion_tokens": 1312, "prompt_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 1616}, {"completion_tokens": 1351, "prompt_tokens": 305, "total_tokens": 1656}, {"completion_tokens": 1490, "prompt_tokens": 308, "total_tokens": 1798}, {"completion_tokens"